SUMMARY:Walls That Witnessed a Revolution: Lancaster County Before 1776
DESCRIPTION:Historic Rock Ford’s America250 Lecture Series presents “Walls That Witnessed a Revolution: Lancaster County Before 1776” in which Danielle Keperling explores the pre-1776 buildings throughout Lancaster County. \n\nThis presentation will begin at 6 PM in the Langmuir Education Room located on the first floor of the Rock Ford Barn. Admission is for the lecture only and does not include the Snyder Gallery or Hand Mansion.\n\nAbout the Presenter: Danielle Keperling serves as the Executive Director of the Historic Preservation Trust of Lancaster County\, where she advances preservation advocacy\, education\, and stewardship across the county. She also serves on the Lancaster City Historical Commission\, helping oversee the Heritage Conservation District. \n            \n        \n                \n            \n                \n                \n    Learn More
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/walls-that-witnessed-a-revolution-lancaster-county-before-1776/
LOCATION:Historic Rock Ford\, 881 ROCKFORD RD\, Lancaster\, 17602
CATEGORIES:Education & Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/05/WallsthatWitnessedaRevolution.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="Historic Rock Ford":MAILTO:office@historicrockford.org
END:VEVENT
