SUMMARY:First Annual Connectivity Day
DESCRIPTION:The Anne Brossman Sweigart Charitable Foundation will host its first annual  community fundraiser\, “Connectivity Day“. The afternoon invites neighbors to a rare visit inside  one of Ephrata’s landmark homes\, with every dollar raised benefiting Ephrata Area Social Services  (EASS).  \n\n\n\nGuests will enjoy local food trucks\, live music\, guided tours of the historic house\, and a raffle. The afternoon opens with a VIP hour from 11:30 to 12:30 p.m.\, welcomes the general public from 1:00 to 3:00 p.m.\, and closes from 3:00 to 4:00 p.m. with a special reunion honoring retirees of the Denver & Ephrata (D&E) Telephone Company. Admission is $10\, with 100% of the proceeds benefitting EASS. Space is limited\, and advance purchase is required. \n\n\n\n\n    Get tickets
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/first-annual-connectivity-day/
LOCATION:204 Spring Garden Street\, Ephrata
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/07/Connectivity-Day-2026-FInal-Flyer-scaled.avif
END:VEVENT
